      <div class="calc-main">
        <h1>📦 Pack Comparison Calculator</h1>
        <p class="calc-intro">Compare two different packs by price and quantity to find out which one offers the lower price per unit.</p>

        <div class="card">
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:1rem">
            <div style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem">
              <p style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.04em;margin-bottom:0.75rem">Pack 1</p>
              <label>Price</label>
              <input type="number" id="pc-price1" step="0.01" min="0" placeholder="e.g. 4.99" oninput="comparePacks()">
              <label>Number of units</label>
              <input type="number" id="pc-quantity1" step="1" min="1" placeholder="e.g. 6" oninput="comparePacks()">
            </div>
            <div style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem">
              <p style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:700;color:#22C55E;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.04em;margin-bottom:0.75rem">Pack 2</p>
              <label>Price</label>
              <input type="number" id="pc-price2" step="0.01" min="0" placeholder="e.g. 6.99" oninput="comparePacks()">
              <label>Number of units</label>
              <input type="number" id="pc-quantity2" step="1" min="1" placeholder="e.g. 10" oninput="comparePacks()">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="result-box" id="pc-res">Enter the price and units of both packs</div>
        </div>

        <div id="pc-desglose" style="display:none;margin-top:1rem">
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0.75rem" id="pc-cards"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem">How to compare two packs</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem">When two products contain different quantities, comparing only the total price can be misleading. A larger pack is not necessarily cheaper per unit.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem">To compare two packs fairly, divide the price of each pack by the number of units it contains. The resulting unit prices can then be compared directly.</p>

          <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem;margin-top:1.25rem">Pack comparison example</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8">If a pack of 6 costs $4.80, each unit costs $0.80. If another pack contains 10 units and costs $7, each unit costs $0.70. The second pack costs more overall, but its price per unit is lower.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="calc-sidebar">
        <div class="card sidebar-card">
          <h2>What is the price per unit?</h2>
          <p>The price per unit is the total price of a pack divided by the number of units it contains. It allows you to compare products sold in different pack sizes on equal terms — regardless of whether one pack contains 6 items and another contains 10.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card sidebar-card">
          <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>
          <details>
            <summary>How does the pack comparison calculator work?</summary>
            <p>Enter the price and number of units in each pack. The calculator divides the price by the number of units and compares the resulting unit prices.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I compare packs with different quantities?</summary>
            <p>Yes. Comparing different pack sizes is one of the main purposes of this calculator.</p>
          </details>
